\frac{W_m}{W} &= \frac{p \frac{1 - q^{mn}}{1 - q^n}}{\frac{p}{1 - q^n}} \\
&= 1 - q^{mn}
\end{align*}$$
Substitute $q = 1 - \frac{1}{n}$:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{W_m}{W} &= 1 - \left(1 - \frac{1}{n}\right)^{mn} \\
&= 1 - \left[\left(1 - \frac{1}{n}\right)^n\right]^m
\end{align*}$$
From part (b), we know $e^{-\frac{n}{n-1}} < \left(1 - \frac{1}{n}\right)^n < e^{-1}$. 
For large $n$, the term $\frac{n}{n-1} = \frac{1}{1 - 1/n} \approx 1$, so the lower bound approaches $e^{-1}$. By the squeeze theorem, for large $n$:
$$\begin{align*}
\left(1 - \frac{1}{n}\right)^n &\approx e^{-1}
\end{align*}$$
Substituting this approximation into the ratio:
$$\begin{align*}
\frac{W_m}{W} &\approx 1 - \left(e^{-1}\right)^m \\
